# How to cite this fork.
#
# Two blocks, two purposes:
#   - the top level describes THIS SOFTWARE (the fork), and is what Zenodo and
#     GitHub's "Cite this repository" button read;
#   - `preferred-citation` names the PAPER that should be cited in the text of a
#     publication, which is the conventional academic credit.
#
# `doi` below is the VERSION DOI of v3.0.0+thesis, not the concept DOI
# (10.5281/zenodo.21774609), so that a citation always resolves to this exact
# snapshot.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this fork, please cite the software entry below and the conference
  paper under `preferred-citation`. Please also cite upstream GNPy
  (doi:10.5281/zenodo.3458319), of which this is a derivative work.
title: "Accelerated GNPy fork with JIT-compiled NLI routines"
abstract: >-
  Fork of GNPy branched from upstream tag v2.13, in which three CPU-bound routines
  of the nonlinear-interference computation are reimplemented with Numba just-in-time
  compilation, leaving the mathematical expressions and physical models unchanged.
  Numerical equivalence with upstream was verified over 30,606 independent WDM and
  EON scenarios, with a maximum relative error of 2.23e-15. Two upstream failure
  modes are also removed: a division by zero for ideal filters and silent NaN
  propagation for vanishing attenuation or dispersion.
type: software
version: 3.0.0+thesis
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21774610"
date-released: "2026-08-03"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheMatheusLs/oopt-gnpy"
keywords:
  - elastic optical networks
  - multiband transmission
  - quality of transmission
  - GSNR
  - GNPy
  - just-in-time compilation
authors:
  - given-names: "Matheus L."
    family-names: "Santos"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8331-1087"
    affiliation: "Federal University of Pernambuco, Recife, Brazil"
    email: "matheus.lobo@ufpe.br"

# O software é derivado do GNPy upstream; a atribuição fica explícita aqui.
# O DOI abaixo é o da VERSÃO v2.13, que é a base real do fork. O concept DOI do
# GNPy (10.5281/zenodo.3458319) resolve sempre para a release mais recente e
# hoje aponta para a v2.14.1, publicada depois deste fork.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "GNPy: Optical Route Planning and DWDM Network Optimization"
    version: "v2.13"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.17207373"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Telecominfraproject/oopt-gnpy"
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    authors:
      - name: "Telecom Infra Project and GNPy contributors"

preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: >-
    A Tabulated GSNR Framework for Tractable QoT-Aware RSA in C+L+S Elastic
    Optical Networks
